<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>I'm Sorry, My Love</title>
  <style>
    body {
      background: linear-gradient(to right, #ffe0e9, #ffe0f7);
      font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
      text-align: center;
      padding: 50px 20px;
      color: #333;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: 3em;
      color: #d6336c;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }

    p {
      font-size: 1.3em;
      max-width: 700px;
      margin: 20px auto;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .heart {
      font-size: 4em;
      color: #ff6b81;
      margin: 20px 0;
      animation: pulse 1.5s infinite;
    }

    @keyframes pulse {
      0% { transform: scale(1); }
      50% { transform: scale(1.1); }
      100% { transform: scale(1); }
    }

    .footer {
      margin-top: 40px;
      font-size: 1em;
      color: #888;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="heart">❤️</div>
  <h1>I'm Sorry, [Her Name]</h1>

  <p>
    I know I hurt you, and I regret every moment of it. My heart feels heavy without you, and I miss everything about us—your smile, your laugh, your presence.
  </p>

  <p>
    I never meant to cause you pain, and I promise to reflect, grow, and become the person you deserve. You mean the world to me, and I hope, in time, you can forgive me.
  </p>

  <p>
    This page is a small piece of my apology—a space where my love for you lives openly and honestly.
  </p>

  <div class="footer">With all my love,<br>[Your Name]</div>

</body>
</html>
